  "title": "Srinivasa Ramanujan",
  "summary": "Born in Erode on 22 December 1887, Ramanujan travelled to Trinity College, Cambridge in 1914 after G. H. Hardy replied to his 1913 letter. The two worked together on partitions, and he was elected a Fellow of the Royal Society in 1918. He died on 26 April 1920, aged 32.",
